  "title": "Room constraints (D9c): a fixed and a forbidden room, travel costs, the nearest-room strategy",
  "notes": [
    "Issue #70, D9c (legacy-parity-inventory.md PAR-055, 056, 060, 061, 063, A-2, Q-30; SQL case 141). One plan and period (2 days x 3 slots); both templates of subject A may use rooms L1, L2 and L3 with priority 1 and share a day (breakdown without order, same day allowed).",
    "Legacy side: the travel costs through the room's travel cost editor (get_form_edit_lugar_costos_de_traslado, then one custom_set_costotraslado per other room, 0 included, as ancoragoh_client_forms_costotraslado.js posts them); the fixed and forbidden rooms, which no screen wrote (A-4), through add_LugarFijo and add_AccesoProhibido. Drupal side: RoomConstraints, the save of the editors.",
    "Group 1 has the fixed room L3 and the forbidden room L1 (which generar() never applies, Q-30). Run E uses buscalugar = TRUE, the legacy window's default (A-2): Group 2 gets the room with the least travel cost from the rooms used around its slot."
  ],
